# @epistemologic/pact/bilateral — the substrate-decl'd shape of a
# bilateral predicate. Species under @epistemologic/pact at the
# machine-readable-shape altitude.
#
# Species under @pact declaring the TYPED CARRIER for what the ~30
# hand-written apply_h::act arms across 8 shard groups (Arc-2 Ticks
# 2.1-2.4 + @sheaf + @uuid/spectral/time + @roomba bump/vacuum +
# @mirror/store gc + @gestalt.annotation) currently duplicate as
# docblock prose + Rust `if action == "X" && arg.oid.contains("Y")`
# arms.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Alex 2026-07-16 in-transcript verbatim (ratification):
#     "Q1. Let's mint it then. Properly. Seems like it's load-bearing."
#
# - Taut Q1 substrate-truth scout (this session, 2026-07-16 evening):
#     NO grammar-decl'd `bilateral <name> { sentinel: "..." }` shape
#     exists. Sentinel string lives in docblock prose ONLY — not
#     extractable via grammar. Closest extensible carrier is
#     `shards/epistemologic/pact/*.mirror` — @pact family already
#     carries "bilateral predicate that holds or fails" as first-class
#     at family altitude. ~30 duplicate arms across 8 shard groups in
#     `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` (~700 LOC of duplication of what shard
#     docblock prose already declares).
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/bilateral-predicate-substrate-shape.md`
#   (Mara THIS-tick; §0-§10; the substrate-decl'd shape + retirement
#   contract + landing plan pointer for Reed's follow-up).
#
# - Math foundation:
#   `docs/math/epistemologic/pact/bilateral-sentinel.md`
#   (Mara THIS-tick; sentinel-as-content-addressed-witness + Connes-
#   triple correspondence for the reflective evaluator).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# The bilateral pattern was substrate-decl'd verbatim across the four
# COLLAPSED Rust files' shard-decl replacements (all landed 2026-07-15
# to 2026-07-16 under Arc-2 Tick 2.1-2.4):
#
#   1. `shards/spectral/signature.mirror` (Arc-2 Tick 2.1 FIRST BITE;
#      commit f211ee48) — 4 bilateral predicates:
#        signature_integrity            → chain=merkle-linked
#        signature_authorship           → authorship=ssh-matched
#        signature_monotone             → ordering=timestamp-monotone
#        signature_composition_honest   → composition=song-emission
#
#   2. `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence.mirror` (Arc-2 Tick
#      2.2 SECOND BITE; Mara e0a3e48) — 4 bilateral predicates:
#        coherence_increases            → axis=splinter-ward
#        is_narcissus_pole              → structure=star-K1n
#        is_splinter_pole               → structure=complete-Kn
#        coherence_witnessing           → witness=coherence-preserving
#
#   3. `shards/peer/persistence.mirror` (Arc-2 Tick 2.3 THIRD BITE) —
#      5 bilateral predicates (4 base + 1 composed):
#        projection_visibility_respected → visibility=filter-respected
#        harvest_consent_verified        → consent=chain-verified
#        boot_state_coherent             → basis=snapshot-matched
#        home_content_addressed          → identity=content-addressed
#        home_witnessing                 → witnessing=all-four-pass
#
#   4. `shards/kintsugi/roomba.mirror` (Arc-2 Tick 2.4 FOURTH BITE) —
#      5 bilateral predicates (4 base + 1 composed):
#        walk_terminates_cleanly         → termination=scope-a-exhaustive
#        tension_monotone_descending     → tension=trajectory-descending
#        coherence_gradient_admissible   → gradient=foerster-admissible
#        knife_verdict_bounded           → verdict=three-state-bounded
#        walk_witnessing                 → witnessing=all-four-pass
#
# Additional siblings (Reed 2026-07-16 Bridge-β extensions):
#   5. `shards/subject/visibility/sheaf.mirror` — 4 bilateral arms
#   6. `shards/uuid/spectral/time.mirror` — 4 bilateral arms (Reed
#      substrate-floor c10a3bd; sbec +4)
#   7. `shards/kintsugi/roomba.mirror` bump/vacuum additive cascade —
#      3+ bilateral arms
#   8. `shards/mirror/store.mirror` gc_reachability_closure_second_
#      witness — 1 bilateral arm
#
# ~30 arms total across 8 shard groups; ~15 LOC per arm direct
# duplication + ~250 LOC error-message prose = ~700 LOC cruft in
# `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs`. This species names the substrate-decl'd
# shape whose reflective evaluator (Reed follow-up tick) replaces the
# entire cruft with ~50 LOC of grammar-loader-composed dispatch.
#
# === The load-bearing claim ===
#
# Every one of the ~30 arms follows the SAME shape:
#
#   if action == "<shard-ref>.<predicate-name>" {
#       if let Some(arg) = args.first() {
#           if arg.oid.contains("<sentinel-string>") {
#               return Verdict::Pass;
#           }
#           return Verdict::Fail(format!(
#               "<predicate-name>: expected <sentinel-string> \
#                sentinel ... got arg oid {:?}", arg.oid,
#           ));
#       }
#       return Verdict::Fail("<predicate-name>: missing argument");
#   }
#
# The only per-arm variability is:
#   (a) the action ref string
#   (b) the sentinel byte-string
#   (c) the human-readable predicate name in the error message
#   (d) the argument arity (1-arg base OR 2-arg composed OR N-arg)
#
# All three (a-c) are ALREADY declared in the shard-decl's docblock
# prose. Only (d) is structural. Making (a-c) machine-readable via a
# typed `bilateral { sentinel: "..." arity: N }` carrier reduces the
# resolver to: grammar-loader reads the shard-decl at parse time,
# extracts every bilateral's sentinel + arity, dispatches generically.
#
# One general Rust implementation (~50 LOC) replaces the ~700 LOC of
# hand-typed arms. sbec neutral (same Pass/Fail verdicts fire against
# the same sentinels); io_violations neutral (no @io); rust_loc -650
# net. ouroboros_monotone four-conjunct HOLDS by construction.
#
# === Grammar-decl'd shape (machine-readable via existing loader) ===
#
# Two new companion keywords via `shards/epistemologic/pact/keywords.
# mirror` registered in `bootstrap/src/grammar.rs::companion_keyword_
# sources` for `shards/mirror/grammar.mirror`:
#
#   focus bilateral    — opens a recursively-scanned brace block
#                         carrying the predicate's typed fields
#                         (sentinel, arity, predicate-name, error-
#                         message-template). Same AstKind::Focus
#                         precedent as `focus project` in @mirror/spec.
#
#   project sentinel   — single-line directive whose payload is the
#                         byte-string sentinel the predicate checks
#                         for. Same AstKind::Project precedent as
#                         `project source` in @mirror/spec.
#
# The bilateral block body:
#
#   bilateral <predicate_name> {
#     sentinel  "<byte-string>"
#     arity     <nat>          -- 1 for base | 2 for composed pairs
#                              --   | N for N-arg bilaterals
#     require   <sub-bilateral>  -- optional; for composed bilaterals
#     require   <sub-bilateral>  --   naming the sub-predicates whose
#                              --   AND-conjunction discharges Pass
#   }
#
# The grammar loader parses the bilateral block into an AST node with
# `sentinel` / `arity` / `require` children. `apply_h::act` reads the
# corpus of parsed bilateral declarations at boot; dispatches by
# looking up `action` against the declared bilateral name; extracts
# `sentinel` + `arity`; byte-checks; discharges. Composed bilaterals
# recursively evaluate their `require` children.
#
# === The bilateral species carrier ===
#
# Per this species: `bilateral` IS the shape a predicate declares to
# be dispatchable via `apply_h::act` reflectively. The shape carries
# four typed fields at declaration time:
#
#   name       — the predicate's identifier; string-shaped;
#                 concatenated with the enclosing shard's @-ref to
#                 form the full action ref the resolver dispatches on.
#
#   sentinel   — the byte-string the predicate checks for containment
#                 of in the argument's ref.oid. Content-addressed
#                 witness per docs/math/epistemologic/pact/bilateral-
#                 sentinel.md §1. Empty string is substrate-ill-formed
#                 (the predicate would trivially Pass on every arg).
#
#   arity      — the number of arguments the predicate takes. Currently
#                 the substrate's ~30 landed bilaterals cover:
#                   arity 1: 24 base bilaterals (single-arg sentinel
#                            check on the sole arg's oid)
#                   arity 2: 2 composed pairs (both args must witness
#                            the same sentinel — precedent per
#                            @mirror/store.gc_reachability_closure_
#                            second_witness at Reed 2026-07-16 Bridge-β)
#                   arity N: 4 composed bilaterals discharging the AND
#                            of N sub-bilaterals (`require` field
#                            carries the sub-predicate references).
#
#   require    — optional list of sub-bilateral references (typed
#                 as `[ref]` — each element resolves to another
#                 bilateral by name). Non-empty when this bilateral is
#                 composed. The reflective evaluator recursively
#                 evaluates each `require` entry; Pass iff all sub-
#                 bilaterals discharge Pass on the same argument.

prism @epistemologic/pact/bilateral {
  focus  bilateral
  project bilateral
  split  bilateral
  shift  bilateral
  settle bilateral
}

# === Typed carrier ===
#
# The record shape carrying one bilateral declaration. Consumed by the
# reflective `apply_h::act` evaluator (Reed follow-up tick per the
# canonical spec's retirement contract §5).
#
# Fields:
#   name          — predicate identifier. Concatenated with enclosing
#                    shard's @-ref (`{shard_ref}.{name}`) forms the
#                    action ref the resolver dispatches on.
#   sentinel      — byte-string content-addressed witness. The
#                    predicate discharges Pass iff every argument's
#                    ref.oid contains this substring. Non-empty
#                    substrate-invariant per shard docblock discipline.
#   arity         — non-negative integer; number of args the predicate
#                    takes. `1` for base; `2` for two-witness composed;
#                    `N` for N-way composed with `require` populated.
#   require       — optional list of sub-bilateral refs (`[ref]`);
#                    non-empty iff this bilateral composes over the
#                    AND-conjunction of the referenced sub-predicates.
#                    None|Empty for base bilaterals.
type bilateral = {
  name:       ref,
  sentinel:   ref,
  arity:      nat,
  require:    [ref],
}

# === Verdict-discharge action (reflective evaluator surface) ===
#
# The action `apply_h::act` calls reflectively per this species'
# canonical retirement contract. Given the parsed bilateral declaration
# + the concrete arguments the dispatcher received, discharges the
# byte-level sentinel check + composed-bilateral recursion.
#
# Semantics (per docs/specs/bilateral-predicate-substrate-shape.md
# §5.2 reflective evaluator pseudocode):
#
#   discharge(decl, args):
#     if decl.arity != len(args):
#       return Fail(format!("{}: expected {} args, got {}",
#                           decl.name, decl.arity, len(args)))
#     if !decl.require.is_empty():
#       # Composed bilateral: recursively evaluate each sub-bilateral
#       # on the SAME argument list; AND-conjunct verdicts.
#       for sub_ref in decl.require:
#         sub_decl = lookup_bilateral(sub_ref)
#         sub_verdict = discharge(sub_decl, args)
#         if sub_verdict != Pass:
#           return sub_verdict  // first Fail wins; preserves error origin
#       return Pass
#     # Base bilateral: byte-check every arg's oid for sentinel
#     # containment.
#     for arg in args:
#       if !arg.oid.contains(decl.sentinel):
#         return Fail(format!("{}: expected sentinel {:?} in arg oid, \
#                              got {:?}", decl.name, decl.sentinel, arg.oid))
#     return Pass
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; the
# Rust FLOOR at `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` (Reed follow-up tick per
# retirement contract §5.3) composes this action over the grammar
# loader's bilateral-declaration corpus.
discharge(decl: bilateral, args: [ref]) -> verdict { \ }

# === Bilateral-shape well-formedness ===
#
# Meta-bilateral: is a `bilateral` declaration itself well-formed at
# the substrate altitude? Discharges Pass iff:
#   (a) name is non-empty
#   (b) sentinel is non-empty (empty sentinel would trivially Pass on
#       every arg — substrate-ill-formed)
#   (c) arity >= 1 (arity 0 = no-arg bilateral has no verdict surface)
#   (d) require is either empty OR every entry resolves to another
#       declared bilateral in the enclosing corpus
#   (e) if require is non-empty, arity must match the sub-bilaterals'
#       arity by construction (all sub-bilaterals evaluate on the same
#       argument tuple)
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `bilateral=well-formed` — the byte-
# level substrate-decl'd marker for this meta-bilateral.
#
# This IS the "bilateral shape checks itself" — the load-bearing
# self-witnessing that makes the substrate substrate-honest at the
# reflective altitude. Meta-bilateral is arity 1 (checks one bilateral
# decl per invocation); the composed corpus-wide check `all_
# bilaterals_well_formed` is a Reed follow-up if empirical need arises.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked; realized reflectively by the Rust FLOOR.
bilateral_well_formed(decl: bilateral) -> verdict { \ }

# === Composition surface (Taut Q1 substrate-truth scout coverage) ===
#
# @epistemologic/pact/bilateral composes with:
#
#   @kintsugi/consent      — verdict authority per shard docblock
