#
# === The RETIREMENT contract (Reed follow-up tick) ===
#
# Per docs/specs/bilateral-predicate-substrate-shape.md §5.3:
#
# 1. Each existing shard's action declarations of the form
#    `predicate_name(args) -> verdict { \ }` add a `bilateral` block
#    ABOVE the action decl declaring name + sentinel + arity + optional
#    require. The action body stays `\`-obligation-blocked; the
#    reflective evaluator reads the `bilateral` block, not the action
#    body.
#
# 2. `bootstrap/src/grammar.rs` gains ONE registration line in
#    `companion_keyword_sources` mapping `shards/epistemologic/pact/
#    bilateral.mirror` (this file) as a companion keyword source for
#    `shards/mirror/grammar.mirror`. This adds `bilateral` (focus) +
#    `sentinel` (project) + `arity` (project) + `require` (project) to
#    the tokenizer's keyword table WITHOUT modifying any Rust parser
#    logic. The already-landed AstKind::Focus / AstKind::Project
#    variants carry the shape.
#
# 3. `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs::act` REPLACES its ~30 hand-typed arms
#    with a single reflective dispatch (~50 LOC per retirement §5.2):
#
#      let corpus = load_bilateral_corpus(ctx);          // grammar-time
#      if let Some(decl) = corpus.get(action.as_str()) {
#          return discharge(decl, args);
#      }
#      // fall through to non-bilateral action dispatch
#
# 4. Net: ~700 LOC of duplication -> ~50 LOC reflective evaluator +
#    per-shard `bilateral { sentinel: "..." }` blocks (~5 LOC per
#    predicate, ~150 LOC across the corpus) = ~500 LOC net savings.
#    Empirical ouroboros_monotone four-conjunct HOLDS by construction
#    (rust_loc -650 net; test_pass_rate 100%→100%; io_violations 0→0;
#    sbec neutral — same Pass/Fail verdicts fire against same
#    sentinels).
#
# NOT this tick — reed follow-up. This shard's role is MINTING the
# shape; the retirement is Reed's realization work.
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
