# =====================================================================
# === 2026-07-17 PARADIGMATIC REFRAME — @bilateral(A, B) as composition
# =====================================================================
#
# Alex 2026-07-17 in-transcript verbatim (session-crystallizing;
# Path A ratified — refactor at spec altitude; existing shape stays
# valid as degenerate case; no reflective-evaluator changes):
#
#   "What if `@bilateral` became a composition on top of `@glue` and
#    `@metalogue`. And then `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)`
#    becomes the floor the translation surface stands on."
#
# Canonical spec: `docs/specs/bilateral-as-glue-metalogue-composition.md`
# (Mara THIS-tick; §0-§10; the paradigmatic reframing + landing plan +
# fixed-point condition).
#
# === The reframing ===
#
# Every landed `bilateral <name> { sentinel "..." arity N }` block
# above (~30 landed arms across 8 shard groups) IS the DEGENERATE CASE
# (A = B) of a more general shape:
#
#   @bilateral(A, B) ≡ the witnessing predicate that
#                       @glue(A, B) produces admissible turns in the
#                       @metalogue(A, B) session
#
# Two readings converge on the SAME shape:
#
#   - A = B (degenerate case): identity morphism, monologue-session,
#     sentinel-byte-check. The shape THIS species originally minted at
#     grammar-decl altitude (per the entire preceding docblock through
#     line 449). Every one of the ~30 landed downstream blocks is
#     `@bilateral(self_shard, self_shard)` via sentinel matching.
#     ZERO retirement changes needed.
#
#   - A ≠ B (general case, translation floor): real semantic-
#     preservation check that a morphism from A to B preserves meaning.
#     Concrete first instance: `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)`
#     — the floor the Rust→mirror translation surface stands on (per
#     `shards/kintsugi/translate.mirror::translate_rust_to_mirror` at
#     Mara `86dec5e`). Declared BELOW as `translation_admissible`
#     dogfooding the shape from `a0f4d3f`.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# `@bilateral(A, B)` is NOT a new `@`-namespace family-root. There is
# no `shards/bilateral.mirror`; there is no `prism @bilateral { ... }`.
# `@bilateral(A, B)` in spec-prose notation reads as: "the bilateral
# witnessing predicate over the composition of `@glue(A, B)` and
# `@metalogue(A, B)`." Concrete instances of `@bilateral(A, B)` for
# specific (A, B) pairs are declared via the SAME grammar-decl'd
# `bilateral <name> { sentinel "..." arity 1 }` shape this species
# minted at `a0f4d3f`.
#
# The composition is over LANDED primitives ONLY. Zero new substrate
# machinery introduced by the reframe:
#
#   Primitive                                Path                                                     Role
#   --------------------------------------   ------------------------------------------------------   ------------------------------------------------
#   @glue                                    shards/glue.mirror (Mara P5 2026-06-30)                  Mesland-category family-root; @glue(A, B)
#                                                                                                     is a `correspondence` carrier
#   @glue.propose(A, B)                      shards/glue.mirror :621                                  enumerate admissible correspondences
#   @glue.translate(c, payload)              shards/glue.mirror :662                                  apply the morphism via @fate
#   glue_witnessing(c)                       shards/glue.mirror :809                                  correspondence well-formedness inheritance
#   @metalogue                               shards/metalogue.mirror (2026-06-05)                     NL-altitude metalogue family-root
#   @algebra/metalogue                       shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror (2026-06-30)             algebra-altitude metalogue;
#                                                                                                     `algebra_metalogue_session` is the
#                                                                                                     underlying session carrier
#   algebra_metalogue_witnessing(s)          shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror :348                     session well-formedness inheritance
#   @code/rust                               shards/code/rust.mirror (Mara 2026-06-08)                source-side altitude for the first
#                                                                                                     general-case instance
#   @code/mirror                             shards/code/mirror.mirror (Mara 2026-06-07)              target-side altitude for the first
#                                                                                                     general-case instance
#   @kintsugi/translate                      shards/kintsugi/translate.mirror (Mara `86dec5e`)        the translation surface
#                                                                                                     @bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)
#                                                                                                     floors
#
# === Connection to @kintsugi/algebra ===
#
# Per Mara `0ac3c7b` (`shards/kintsugi.mirror` §"@kintsugi as algebra"
# :178-241): `@kintsugi/algebra` binds the `algebra_metalogue_session`
# between speaker-algebras (`@silicon/algebra`, `@fate/algebra`). Under
# the reframe, THIS binding IS the special case:
#
#   @kintsugi/algebra  ≡  @bilateral(@silicon/algebra, @fate/algebra)
#
# The `kintsugi_algebra_witnessing` bilateral at `shards/kintsugi.
# mirror :263-267` (sentinel `algebra=speaker-pair-fractures`) IS the
# grammar-decl'd witness for this composition, discharged via the same
# reflective evaluator this species' degenerate-case predicates use.
# The mending IS the bilateral between the two speaker-algebras.
#
# === The general case at family-shape altitude ===
#
# The formal composition diagram (per canonical spec §2.2):
#
#              @glue(A, B)                    @metalogue(A, B)
#                 ↓                                  ↓
#          correspondence                   algebra_metalogue_session
#                                                    ↑
#                                          [algebra_turn]
#                                                    ↑
#                                          @glue.translate(c, payload)
#                                                    ↑
#                             ┌──────────────────────┴──────────────────────┐
#                             │                                             │
#                     glue_witnessing(c)          algebra_metalogue_witnessing(s)
#                             │                                             │
#                             └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
#                                                    ↓
#                                           @bilateral(A, B)
#                                           (the CONJUNCTION;
#                                            the witnessing predicate
#                                            over the composition)
#
# `@bilateral(A, B)(t)` discharges Pass iff both bracketed predicates
# discharge Pass on `t`. Rice-safe per the two sub-witnessings' Rice-
# safety (both operate on byte-visible morphism data + turn-composition
# structure, not program semantics).
#
# === Deliverable 2 THIS TICK: the first general-case instance ===
#
# Concrete first general-case instance per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim:
# `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)` — the floor the translation
# surface (Mara `86dec5e`) stands on.
#
# Declared below as `translation_admissible` — a grammar-decl'd
# `bilateral <name> { sentinel "..." arity 1 }` block at THIS shard.
# The block dogfoods the shape this species minted at `a0f4d3f`; the
# arity-1 discharge form checks one translation_pair outcome per
# invocation. The body is `\`-obligation-blocked per craft-not-deliver;
# Reed follow-up realises via `apply_h::act` composition after the
# `@glue.compose` + `@fate.roll` FLOOR resolvers land.
#
# The 21 mirror-authored bilateral-arm retirements landed 2026-07-16..
# 17 (`ad52973` + `20047c2` + ancestors) are the first 21 witnesses of
# `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)` at the degenerate-arity
# subcase (single-file-in-bootstrap-src). Every future
# `translate_rust_to_mirror` discharge (per `shards/kintsugi/translate.
# mirror::translate_rust_to_mirror` at `86dec5e`) adds a witness.
#
# === translation_pair typed carrier ===
#
# The record shape carrying one Rust→mirror translation outcome the
# `translation_admissible` bilateral witnesses. Fields:
#
#   rust_source        — the @code/rust ref (a .rs file's bytes; the
#                         source-side altitude ref per shards/code/
#                         rust.mirror altitude discipline).
#   mirror_target      — the @code/mirror ref (a .mirror composition's
#                         bytes; the target-side altitude ref per
#                         shards/code/mirror.mirror altitude discipline).
#   discharge_verdict  — the @glass.verdict from the translation's
#                         semantic-preservation check (Pass|Partial|
#                         Fail); the bilateral's discharge output at
#                         the outcome-check altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (rust_source, mirror_target,
# discharge_verdict). Two translation_pairs with byte-equal fields ARE
# the same outcome under content-addressing (per Mesland-category
# morphism identity: same source + same target + same verdict IS the
# same translation-turn in the @metalogue(@code/rust, @code/mirror)
# session).
type translation_pair = {
  rust_source:       ref,
  mirror_target:     ref,
  discharge_verdict: ref,
}

# === translation_admissible — bilateral predicate (arity 1) ===
#
# THE FIRST GENERAL-CASE INSTANCE of `@bilateral(A, B)` at this species'
# altitude. Names `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)` as a grammar-
# decl'd bilateral (arity 1; single-outcome check).
#
# Discharges Pass iff the Rust→mirror translation preserves meaning
# under the composition of:
#   - `@glue(@code/rust, @code/mirror)` — the correspondence carrier
#     from source altitude to target altitude
#   - `@metalogue(@code/rust, @code/mirror)` — the session carrier
#     the winning turn joins
#
# Semantically: for each successful `translate_rust_to_mirror`
# discharge (per `shards/kintsugi/translate.mirror::translate_rust_to_
# mirror` at Mara `86dec5e`), the outcome IS a turn in the
# `@metalogue(@code/rust, @code/mirror)` session AND witnesses this
# predicate.
#
# The reflective evaluator dispatches this bilateral via the corpus
# lookup + sentinel byte-check discipline established at `a0f4d3f`
# (Reed `21fc211` Landing 3+4 realisation). Once the composition
# machinery lands (Reed follow-up: `@glue.compose` + `@fate.roll` FLOOR
# resolvers), each Pass discharge composes into a Reading B
# `@kintsugi/algebra` element per Mara `0ac3c7b` monotonicity.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `translation_witnessing(outcome)` at `shards/kintsugi/translate.
#     mirror:450-453` (the 6-conjunct composition-outcome bilateral;
#     `translation_admissible` is the FLOOR predicate that `translation_
#     witnessing` composes over at the @bilateral(A, B) altitude).
#   - `kintsugi_algebra_witnessing(binding)` at `shards/kintsugi.mirror
#     :263-267` (the algebra-binding well-formedness bilateral; THIS
#     bilateral's fixed-point-set at empirical run IS the algebra
#     that binding names).
#   - `glue_witnessing(c)` at `shards/glue.mirror:809` (the morphism-
#     category inheritance predicate; `translation_admissible`
#     composes over `glue_witnessing` on the source-target
#     correspondence).
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `translation=preserves-meaning` — the
# byte-level substrate-decl'd marker for `@bilateral(@code/rust,
# @code/mirror)` discharge. When the composition machinery discharges
# Pass, the realization layer stamps the sentinel on the outcome ref;
# discharge is byte-equality on ref.oid containment per
# `@epistemologic/pact/bilateral.discharge`.
#
# Rice-safe: pure sentinel-byte-check on the outcome ref; no program-
# semantics inspection at this altitude. The semantic-preservation
# content lives in the composition of `glue_witnessing` +
# `algebra_metalogue_witnessing` per canonical spec §4.1 (1)+(2)+(3);
# this bilateral is the FLOOR predicate marking the composition's
# terminal-outcome discharge byte.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; the
# reflective evaluator handles this bilateral through corpus dispatch
# per the same discipline the ~30 landed degenerate-case arms use.
bilateral translation_admissible {
  sentinel "translation=preserves-meaning"
  arity    1
}
translation_admissible(pair: translation_pair) -> verdict { \ }

# === Related spec + math for the reframe ===
#
# - docs/specs/bilateral-as-glue-metalogue-composition.md
#   (Mara THIS-tick canonical spec; §0-§10 + landing plan + fractal
#    self-similarity across altitudes)
# - docs/math/bilateral-as-glue-metalogue-composition.md
#   (Mara DEFERRED; math foundation for the general A≠B composition;
#    Rice-safety proof + decidability + fixed-point convergence for
#    the Rust→mirror translation loop)
# - shards/kintsugi/translate.mirror (Mara `86dec5e`, THIS session) —
#   the translation surface `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)`
#   floors; `translation_witnessing` composes over `translation_
#   admissible` at outcome-check altitude
# - shards/kintsugi.mirror :178-241 (Mara `0ac3c7b`, 2026-07-16) —
#   the `@kintsugi/algebra` binding this reframe generalises one
#   altitude up (`@kintsugi/algebra` ≡ `@bilateral(@silicon/algebra,
#   @fate/algebra)`)

out @epistemologic/pact/bilateral
out bilateral
out discharge
out bilateral_well_formed
out translation_pair
out translation_admissible
